Known failure: private local buffer between two FIFO channels
==========================================================

Status: UNRESOLVED; excluded from positive regression counts.
Reproducer: Light_HLS/Tests/LocalWriteData/known_failures/private_stream_buffer.cpp
Top: local_dataflow
Target: U250, 100 MHz

The committed reproducer retains the failing source with an explanatory comment.
Raw logs and generated intermediates preserve the original source paths/content.

Event-loss evidence
-------------------
The local hls::stream stub represents read/write as ordinary load/store.
The initial top.bc for private_buffer already contains:

  entry:
    load i32, ptr %loaded
    add loaded_value, %seed
    branch to initialization loop
  initialization loop:
    store the same value into each buffer element
  exit:
    load buffer[15]
    load buffer[31]
    store their sum to %computed

The source instead requests 32 reads from loaded and 16 writes to computed.
The two surrounding tasks retain 32 produced and 16 consumed items.
This transformation happens before independent scheduling/binding/RTL generation.

Previous compiler fbe1e73f68f671f040aa636ac496511d4ce567ebeb231ef3550be870307de8cd:
  df-check-before: exit 1
  BACKEND_DATAFLOW_RATE_MISMATCH: computed produces 1, consumes 16.
  BACKEND_DATAFLOW_RATE_MISMATCH: loaded produces 32, consumes 1.

Development assertion
---------------------
local-write-v4/local_dataflow and df-check-current abort with SIGABRT.
The recorded caller chain includes:

  llvm::dyn_cast<llvm::SCEVConstant>:
    Assertion `detail::isPresent(Val) && "dyn_cast on a non-existent value"' failed.
  llvm::ScalarEvolution::proveNoWrapViaConstantRanges
  llvm::ScalarEvolution::createSimpleAffineAddRec
  llvm::ScalarEvolution::createAddRecFromPHI
  llvm::ScalarEvolution::computeExitLimitFromICmp
  llvm::ScalarEvolution::computeBackedgeTakenCount
  llvm::ScalarEvolution::getSmallConstantTripCount
  dynamicExecutionCount
  accessRate
  HI_DataflowPerformanceAnalysis::runOnModule

An isolated GDB run (df-gdb/gdb.log) instead returns the rate-mismatch errors.
At each sampled accessRate call, the Function and ScalarEvolution::F addresses
match, as do the LoopInfo and ScalarEvolution::LI addresses. This does not prove
all analysis lifetimes are correct, but does not support a wrong-function-owner
claim. The assertion's root cause and relationship to earlier intermittent
assertions remain unproven. No assertion fix is claimed in this checkpoint.

Retained artifacts
------------------
/tmp/lighthls-local-mux-qor-20260918.4T7n35/local-write-v4/local_dataflow/
/tmp/lighthls-local-mux-qor-20260918.4T7n35/df-check-before/
/tmp/lighthls-local-mux-qor-20260918.4T7n35/df-check-current/
/tmp/lighthls-local-mux-qor-20260918.4T7n35/df-gdb/

The final positive local_dataflow fixture is a different, explicitly documented
PIPO-array design with private RAM and controlled task-clock stalls. Its passing
result is not evidence that private-buffer FIFO event preservation works.
